{"id":"u-67005054-2c7f-40a9-b0db-6e2a149f3bb1","src":"community","title":"JN Push Pull Legs Upper Lower PPLUL","author":"Johnathan","url":"https://www.boostcamp.app/users/uu1fo4-jn-push-pull-legs-upper-lower-ppul","desc":"This five-day Push-Pull-Legs-Upper-Lower (PPLUL) split synthesizes current hypertrophy research into a highly efficient training week. By combining the stabilization and safety of Smith machine compound lifts with the constant tension of cable stations and the versatility of free weights, the program ensures every muscle group is stimulated from multiple joint angles with optimal volume and frequency.\n\nThe routine leans heavily on evidence-based training principles, requiring meticulous tracking of exertion through the RPE (Rate of Perceived Exertion) scale. Early working sets are calculated to leave one to two reps in reserve, preserving energy and ensuring high-quality movement, while the final sets are systematically pushed to absolute technical failure. To maximize the growth stimulus, advanced techniques—specifically lengthened partials and rest-pause sets—are strategically programmed when the target muscles are in their most stretched, high-torque positions. The dual-structure design, blending a traditional PPL block with an Upper/Lower sequence, allows for balanced recovery, varied exercise selection, and comprehensive, systemic muscular development.","level":["Intermediate"],"goals":["Muscle"],"equipment":["Garage Gym"],"minutes":90,"joins":1,"rate":0,"rateCount":0,"updated":"2026-10-02T23:54:19.919Z","variations":[{"name":"default","days":["Push","Pull","Legs","Upper","Lower"],"weeks":[[{"ex":[{"n":"Bench Press (Barbell)","sets":[{"lo":6,"hi":8,"rpe":8,"rpeHi":9,"x":3}],"note":"Focus on a slight arch and pause on the chest."},{"n":"Overhead Press (Machine)","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":12,"rpe":8,"rpeHi":10,"x":3}],"note":"Stability allows safe pushing."},{"n":"Chest Fly (Cable)","sets":[{"lo":10,"hi":15,"rpe":9,"rpeHi":10,"x":3}],"note":"Sets 1–2 RPE 9, last set RPE 10+ with 4–5 lengthened partials."},{"n":"Lateral Raise (Cable)","sets":[{"lo":10,"hi":15,"rpe":9,"rpeHi":10,"x":3}],"note":"Sets 1–2 RPE 9, last set RPE 10."},{"n":"Overhead Tricep Extension (Cable)","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":12,"rpe":9,"rpeHi":10,"x":3}],"note":"Go heavy and emphasize the stretch."},{"n":"Tricep Kickback","sets":[{"lo":12,"hi":15,"rpe":9,"rpeHi":10,"x":2}],"note":"Go lighter and emphasize the squeeze."}]},{"ex":[{"n":"Lat Pulldown (Close Grip)","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":12,"rpe":9,"x":3}],"note":"Vertical torso, massive stretch at the top."},{"n":"Chest Supported Row (Machine)","sets":[{"lo":10,"hi":12,"rpe":9,"x":3}],"note":"Keep elbows flared to hit mid-back."},{"n":"Seated Row (Cable)","sets":[{"lo":10,"hi":12,"rpe":9,"rpeHi":10,"x":3}],"note":"Sets 1–2 RPE 9, last set RPE 10+ with lengthened partials."},{"n":"Rear Delt Fly (Cable)","sets":[{"lo":15,"hi":20,"rpe":9,"rpeHi":10,"x":3}],"note":"Light weight to avoid trap takeover."},{"n":"Shrug (Barbell)","sets":[{"lo":10,"hi":15,"rpe":9,"rpeHi":10,"x":3}],"note":"Shrug up and in toward the ears."},{"n":"Bicep Curl (EZ Bar)","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":12,"rpe":9,"rpeHi":10,"x":3}]},{"n":"Preacher Curl (Machine)","sets":[{"lo":10,"hi":15,"rpe":10,"x":2}],"note":"RPE 10 (Failure)."}]},{"ex":[{"n":"Seated Hamstring Curl","sets":[{"lo":10,"hi":15,"rpe":9,"rpeHi":10,"x":3}],"note":"Do these first to warm up knees for squats."},{"n":"Squat (Smith Machine)","sets":[{"lo":6,"hi":10,"rpe":8,"rpeHi":10,"x":3}]},{"n":"Romanian Deadlift (Barbell)","sets":[{"lo":6,"hi":8,"rpe":8,"rpeHi":9,"x":3}],"note":"Use straps; do not let grip limit the set."},{"n":"Leg Extension","sets":[{"lo":10,"hi":15,"rpe":9,"rpeHi":10,"x":2}],"note":"Sets 1–2 RPE 9, last set RPE 10+ with Rest-pause 3 more reps."},{"ss":[{"n":"Hip Adductor (Machine)","sets":[{"lo":12,"hi":15,"rpe":9,"rpeHi":10,"x":2}],"note":"Superset directly with Abductions."},{"n":"Hip Abductor (Machine)","sets":[{"lo":12,"hi":15,"rpe":9,"rpeHi":10,"x":2}]}